author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A sandboxed workspace neutralizes harness signal environment, so recorded provenance depends only on the harness the fixture declares and never on the process running the suite; A provenance resolver reads only environment variables belonging to the harness whose descriptor matched, so a codex descriptor never consumes a value written by another tool; The outcome classifier distinguishes a resolver that was handed valid input and failed from one that was handed another harness's value, so the record never reports resolver_failed for input that was never the harness's to begin with; The agent-runtime-primitives expectation holds with AI_AGENT unset, set to a value carrying a parseable version, and set to a value that does not, proving the verdict no longer varies with the host; Local preflight carries a control that sets a foreign harness variable and fails if any spec's verdict changes, so this divergence class cannot silently return"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Hardened test sandboxes against only the ambiguous foreign AI_AGENT signal and taught shared resolver attribution to ignore a literal signal belonging to another detected harness.
expected_result: "Foreign ambient harness metadata must not contaminate SDK or CLI attribution, while explicit same-harness and dedicated resolver signals remain testable."
actual_result: "Codex attribution ignores a Claude-valued shared AI_AGENT variable; sandbox helpers clear ambiguous AI_AGENT without erasing dedicated harness variables, preserving CLI/MCP parity coverage."
