comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T13:48:46.953Z","harness:claude-code","Reproduction, exact and cheap, recorded 2026-08-09 at commit 9a0a048b6. Filed only; not fixed in this pass.\n\nFailing run, with the harness variable present as an agent would have it:\n\n  node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/agent-runtime-primitives.spec.ts\n\nfails one of sixteen, at agent-runtime-primitives.spec.ts:741, on attributes update and close mutations to the detected harness. Both compared history entries carry an unexpected context.agent_provenance_outcomes.version block reading status failed, reason resolver_failed, resolver ai_agent_version, rule_version v1.\n\nPassing run, identical in every other respect:\n\n  env -u AI_AGENT node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/agent-runtime-primitives.spec.ts\n\npasses sixteen of sixteen. One variable is the entire difference, and it is a variable the fixture never sets and never refers to.\n\nThe host value on this machine is claude-code_2-1-226_agent. It matters that this string is not malformed: the resolver's regex requires the version at the end of the string, and this value ends in the literal text agent, so a perfectly ordinary harness value fails to parse. An agent whose AI_AGENT happened to end in a version would produce a third outcome again, which is why the acceptance criteria ask for all three forms to be exercised rather than only the unset case.\n\nChain of custody through the source, so the fix has three separable candidate sites rather than one guess. src/core/shared/author.ts:219 declares the codex descriptor's version resolver as ai_agent_version. src/core/shared/author.ts:569 implements that resolver by reading env.AI_AGENT, a name several harnesses write, with no check that the value belongs to the harness that matched. src/core/shared/author.ts:897 classifies the outcome, and decides between failed and unavailable by asking only whether env.AI_AGENT is non-blank; presence of any value is taken as evidence that the resolver had legitimate input, which is what converts an honest unavailable into a misleading failed.\n\nConfirmation that this is not a flake and not caused by the change shipped alongside it. The failure appeared first inside a full coverage run and then reproduced identically in isolation, and it reproduces on every invocation with the variable set. Two other specs failed in that same coverage run, governance-read-performance and surface-replication-gate, and both pass cleanly when re-run without concurrent load; those two are wall-clock sensitive and are not this. Continuous integration is green at this commit, which is consistent with hosted runners setting no AI_AGENT.\n\nScope note on what this does and does not touch. The two history entries are otherwise correct: author is harness:codex, author_source is detected, and the patch contents are as expected. The leak affects the provenance outcome block only. That is what makes it a containment question rather than a correctness question about detection, and it is why the item is parented on continuous integration rather than on the identity lineage, while still citing that lineage.\n"
  "2026-08-09T15:26:24.456Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: sandbox isolation now clears only the ambiguous shared AI_AGENT signal; explicit CODEX/Claude session signals remain available for intentional CLI/MCP parity. The foreign AI_AGENT reproducer and mutation-envelope parity suite both pass."
  "2026-08-09T15:57:29.521Z","harness:codex","Evidence: both linked test groups passed; final full suite passed 7,100/7,100 with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; pnpm lint and all static quality gates passed. The narrowed isolation behavior is documented in the item history and avoids masking dedicated resolver fixtures."
